{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05d034de3719a5ba616f909e520606defa633fb7690abce437bb3a873234c485"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs a web UI on localhost:3000 with email one-time-passcode or Google login, and credentials are stored in persistent-data/auth/userKeyMap.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_273fa2ca809abaddb82e1688ee6d8ee3ec8003a89d602393f3b792a0014d3d4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Training is triggered by pressing Ctrl+C in the terminal; the system compares user edits to assistant actions, computes rewards and penalties, updates a local checkpoint, and stores weights under persistent-data/trainer/models."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3fd9ea0667807a7a4caec04b9f927c74d0b4f5e968c65b2b7f394bec7eca78d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The assistant writes directly in the user's editor; every keystroke, edit, or deletion acts as a learning signal so it adapts to the user's habits over time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_656c77976c11e92acad28941ae64ce09c72564c6c6a12f7f3de60cd5292f5b60"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README notes that new CodeAssist participation on Testnet is no longer tracked as the team shifts focus to Mainnet, though historical data remains on-chain."},{"claim_ids":["clm_79b5722ed17d48039954d33dd9f7e389bc810d96b0357c17e687e49fff4a814e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users select Easy, Medium, or Hard problems from a sidebar, and the assistant can be paused via Shift+Space or a Pause button, with a 'No-Op' signaling the user's turn."},{"claim_ids":["clm_81ffc565586c212c42fc7864a258e6e1dfc3de7417eb0bb16a0023d327195468"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors use a pre-commit hook for linting and ruff format; commits failing Ruff checks fail GitHub actions and must be fixed before merging."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88ad0ac9efb7579a7902a85a0172153b67651f0e5e24851b7840edfc58e826f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product's improvement loop is user-driven: README guidance suggests improvement becomes clearer after roughly 4-5 training episodes, implying no automated benchmark harness is documented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a99fd65a56809281d9b4c2e26c4f312cc8de45cfdec263be91aba42342ef7472"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented troubleshooting covers unhealthy containers (viewable via docker logs), Docker daemon connection errors, and port 3000 conflicts, with ports 8000, 8080, 8001, 8008, 3003, and 11434 reserved for other services."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d91e5f2c9eb57bb50c57523f22435f0eb06cc58abd0f1f84d7e05704c0c2726f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CodeAssist is described as a fully private, local AI coding assistant by Gensyn that helps users practice programming problems and train a personal assistant."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de31052833cec99e4894c5ad6ae2d289970bda0682b056894965b14a684afd9b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The main script is run with 'uv run run.py', which handles the environment and launches the assistant; a --port argument can override the default port 3000."},{"claim_ids":["clm_efce536500807093090219eec8da40d6d864f1f2d597928ece7d8384c411ffc2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Episodes need not solve the problem successfully; users can stop recording by leaving the web UI and starting training with ctrl+c, and the trained model uploads to Hugging Face if a valid token exists."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1e6093d9ee077f5404a15d4319cdde8e2fd55c2d17b3b259cc383ba89a1f9c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running CodeAssist requires Docker, Python no older than 3.10, and UV for dependency management, plus a HuggingFace token with Write access."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05d034de3719a5ba616f909e520606defa633fb7690abce437bb3a873234c485","clm_273fa2ca809abaddb82e1688ee6d8ee3ec8003a89d602393f3b792a0014d3d4f","clm_3fd9ea0667807a7a4caec04b9f927c74d0b4f5e968c65b2b7f394bec7eca78d6","clm_656c77976c11e92acad28941ae64ce09c72564c6c6a12f7f3de60cd5292f5b60","clm_79b5722ed17d48039954d33dd9f7e389bc810d96b0357c17e687e49fff4a814e","clm_81ffc565586c21